            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for to cuddle, then the Malayalam for a get-together."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കുശലം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുശലം — kuśalaṁ — \"pleasantries; small talk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വഴിയിൽ കണ്ട അയൽക്കാരനോട് അച്ഛൻ കുശലം ചോദിച്ചു. vaḻiyil kaṇṭa ayalkkāranōṭŭ acchan kuśalaṁ cōdiccu. Father asked after the neighbour he met on the road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുശലം (kuśalaṁ) ചോദിക്കുക, to ask after someone, is the set phrase."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുശലം (kuśalaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit kuśala, \"right, proper, healthy\" (CDIAL 3365): to ask the കുശലം is to ask whether all is well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
