          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കൊഞ്ചുക — koñcuka — \"to prattle; to talk baby talk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുഞ്ഞ് അമ്മയോട് കൊഞ്ചി. kuññŭ ammayōṭŭ koñci. The baby babbled sweetly to its mother."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past: കൊഞ്ചി, koñci."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also the cooing of grown-ups to a baby; കൊഞ്ചൽ is the noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കൊഞ്ചുക (koñcuka) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2043 gives the Malayalam verb as to prattle and to fondle, as with a child (DEDR 2043)."
            }
          ]
