          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുതിർന്ന — mutirnna — \"grown-up; senior\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വീട്ടിലെ മുതിർന്ന ആളുകളെ കുട്ടികൾ ബഹുമാനിക്കണം. vīṭṭile mutirnna āḷukaḷe kuṭṭikaḷ bahumānikkaṇaṁ. Children should respect the grown-ups at home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുതിർന്നവർ means the elders, the adults."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുതിർന്ന (mutirnna) is native Dravidian, the adjective of മുതിരുക, \"to grow ripe, to mature\", which DEDR 4954 lists with മുതു, \"old\" (DEDR 4954)."
            }
